We also need to consider that some actions require candidate_task_profile_linked (like confirm_candidate_preparedness? Not needed). For origin we need candidate_task_profile_linked for activate_origin_node, unload_origin_payload, etc. Actually activate_origin_node requires candidate_task_profile_linked. Unload_origin_payload also requires candidate_task_profile_linked. So we need task profile linked for origin during its activate and unload steps. So we need to have it linked at those times. So we need to have it linked for origin during activate and unload, and also for destination during activate and unload. So we need to switch.

Thus we can do: attach to origin, do origin activate, load, unload (needs task profile for unload). Then detach from origin, attach to destination, do destination activate, load, unload (needs task profile for unload). Then detach from destination, attach to origin (final). At the end origin has task profile linked.

Alternatively we could keep task profile linked to origin throughout origin steps, then detach, attach to destination for its steps, detach, reattach to origin. That's fine.

Now also need candidate_operator_linked for lock actions. We'll assign operator to origin before lock, then release after lock, assign to destination before lock, release after lock.

Now also need cargo_available for loading. Initially cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha true. After loading origin, cargo becomes unavailable. After unload origin, cargo becomes available again. Then we can load destination (cargo needed). After loading destination, cargo unavailable. After unload destination, cargo becomes available again (not needed). So we need to ensure cargo is available when we load each.

Now also need to ensure we have loading_container linked? Not required for goal. However some actions like activate_origin_node etc do not require loading container. So we can ignore loading container.

Now also need to ensure we have transport leg assembled. For assemble_transport_leg we need origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available. We'll have those after we complete origin and destination sequences (including lock/unload). Also need transport_leg_available (init true). After assemble, transport_leg_available becomes false.

Now also need transport_leg_origin_linked and transport_leg_destination_linked (effects of assemble). Good.

Now we also need vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (we will allocate). Also need vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma (we will get from schedule dispatch). Also need dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (we will do execute_schedule_dispatch). Also need dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha (we will get from execute_schedule_dispatch effect). Good.

Now also need candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha and origin_availability_alpha (we will prepare them). Also need candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta (after allocation). Also need origin_availability_confirmed and locked (we will get). Also need destination_availability_confirmed and locked (we will get). Also need origin_node_occupied and ready, destination_node_occupied and ready (we will get via load/unload). Also need transport_leg_assembled and links (after assemble). Also need vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (after allocation). Also need vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma (after schedule dispatch). Also need dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha (after schedule dispatch). Also need dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (after schedule dispatch). Also need candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha? Not in goal but we already have it true initially.

Now we must ensure we don't violate any preconditions.

